FFmpeg (LGPL build) bundled with EdgeSlicer on Linux
====================================================

The file `ffmpeg` in this folder is an unmodified, statically linked build of FFmpeg @DESC@ for @ARCH@,
made by the BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds project and redistributed here as a separate program. EdgeSlicer's phone hub
runs it as a child process (through go2rtc) to re-encode camera streams for the phone's Quality steps; it is
not linked into EdgeSlicer.

Licence: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (the text is in FFMPEG-LICENSE.txt in this folder).
The build is configured with --enable-version3 and WITHOUT --enable-gpl or --enable-nonfree, and with
--disable-libx264 --disable-libx265, so it contains no GPL components. Its software H.264 encoder is
libopenh264 (Cisco OpenH264, BSD-2-Clause). It also contains other free libraries that BtbN's build
statically links (dav1d, libvpx, opus, freetype, zlib, OpenSSL and others); their licences are those of
the respective projects, listed with the build scripts below.

Where it came from
  Release:   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/@TAG@
  Archive:   @ASSET@
  SHA-256:   @SHA256@
  Build recipe (every library, version and patch used): https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds (scripts.d/ and
             patches/ at the commit this release was built from, shown on the release page)

Corresponding source
  FFmpeg:    https://git.ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.git, commit @COMMIT@ (release branch 8.1, `git describe`: @DESC@).
             Browse: https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/@COMMIT@
  The other libraries: from their own projects, at the versions named in the BtbN scripts above.

Written offer
  If you received this EdgeSlicer package and want the source code of the FFmpeg build in it, or help
  replacing it with a build of your own (the hub uses whatever executable is at this path), contact the
  EdgeSlicer maintainers through https://github.com/aceRage/EdgeSlicer/issues and ask for the FFmpeg source;
  it will be sent for three years from the date of the release you received, at no charge beyond the cost of
  the medium if one is needed. You may also replace the `ffmpeg` file with any other build: EdgeSlicer
  only needs an executable named ffmpeg with the libopenh264 encoder here, and falls back to a system ffmpeg
  or to no re-encoding when it is missing.

